On Fri, 28 Jul 2006, Jove wrote:

>   - Do NOT be burdened.  Learn to stash early and often.

In particular, there are some items which you just do not need until far
in the future, so you can stash them in monster-inaccessible areas (first
level of Sokoban; for scrolls to be blanked or rings to be polymorphed) or
sell them to shopkeepers (spellbooks, certain wands).

Other items (such as unidentified scrolls or potions) can be carried in a
bag (safe of fire), so that they are at hand when you get a scroll of
identify or see a throne.


It has been said before that using the "Get out of Jail"-cards is an
important part of any strategy, and this certainly was what improved my
playing style the most. For a long time, I hesitated to use my precious
wand of lightning on that ant, because it could be of greater use later
on; and died subsequently to the ant, leaving the wand completely useless
to a dead character.

In general, /spend/ your resources. They are not in the game to be horded.
Fire at the foes with whatever you have available, and if it is a wand of
death for a killer bee, so be it.

